{"id":1360,"date":"2020-11-26T20:05:04","date_gmt":"2020-11-27T04:05:04","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1360"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:51","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:51","slug":"rokit-random","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/rokit-random\/","title":{"rendered":"Random"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221645aea01\" name=\"6a221645aea01\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>How to program random()<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Programming is usually very predictable. The same things happen at the same time, and if that part of the program is in a\u00a0<em>loop<\/em>, those things will happen over and over again. But what if you don&#8217;t want to know what&#8217;s going to happen? What if you&#8217;re using a Magic 8 ball app, or if you&#8217;re programming a Clapping Monkey Bot to wait a random amount of time before clapping its hands? In those cases, you will probably want to use randomization.<\/p>\n<p>There are two different ways to create a random value:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int value = random(max);<\/pre>\n<p>or<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int value = random(min, max);<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221645aeb4b\" name=\"6a221645aeb4b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Use random()<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]These are the differences between the two:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>random(max) will pick a value from 0 up to, but not including, the number you put as the maximum value. For example, if you have a maximum value of 10, the program will pick any number from 0 to 9.<\/li>\n<li>random(min, max) will pick a value between your minimum number and up to, but not including, your maximum number. For example, if you have a minimum value of 5 and a maximum value of 10, the program will pick any number from 5 to 9.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Check out the example code to see how random() can be used with if and else if statements. This code has an output for every number that can be selected.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int choice;\r\n \r\nvoid setup() {\r\n Serial.begin(9600); \/\/ start the Serial monitor\r\n}\r\n \r\nvoid loop() {\r\n\r\n\/\/ pick a random number from 0-4 (not including 4)\r\n choice = random(4); \r\n \/\/ print out a message depending on the random number\r\n if(choice == 0)\r\n {\r\n   Serial.println(\"Hi\");\r\n }\r\n else if (choice == 1)\r\n {\r\n   Serial.println(\"Bye\");\r\n }\r\n else if (choice == 2)\r\n {\r\n   Serial.println(\"Good morning\");\r\n }\r\n else if (choice == 3)\r\n {\r\n   Serial.println(\"Good night\");\r\n }\r\n \r\n delay(500); \/\/ slow it down to watch what is happening\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221645aebc5\" name=\"6a221645aebc5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Example output<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]So what&#8217;s going on with the code?<\/p>\n<p>The program is designed to randomly pick a number between 0 and 4 (but not including 4!). Once the number is picked, the program uses if and else if statements to print a message in the serial monitor. After about half a second, the program will run again!<\/p>\n<p>This is what the serial monitor&#8217;s screen could look like after running the program:<\/p>\n<p>Good night<\/p>\n<p>Bye<\/p>\n<p>Bye<\/p>\n<p>Good morning<\/p>\n<p>Good morning<\/p>\n<p>Hi<\/p>\n<p>Hi<\/p>\n<p>Good morning<\/p>\n<p>Good night<\/p>\n<p>Bye<\/p>\n<p>Hi<\/p>\n<p>Bye<\/p>\n<p>Hi<\/p>\n<p>Good morning<\/p>\n<p>Good night[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221645aec18\" name=\"6a221645aec18\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Still not sure about randomization? Watch the video![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=01OteQY7OW8&#8243; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 5 How to program random() [vc_column_text]Programming is usually very predictable. The same things happen at the same time, and if that part of the program is in a\u00a0loop,&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/rokit-random\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1739,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1760,1777,1808,1793,626,1533,1438,144,209],"lesson-tag":[2163,2123,2219,2122,2171],"class_list":["post-1360","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-monkey-bot","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","module-monkey","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1360","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":3,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1360\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":6620,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1360\/revisions\/6620"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1739"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1360"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1360"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1360"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}